  "A CDN is a fleet of caches close to users. Whether it helps depends entirely on the **cache key** (what makes two requests 'the same') and the **headers** you send. Get them right and the CDN serves most of your traffic; get them wrong and it either does nothing or, worse, serves one user's page to another.",
